==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|crepere}}, from {{inh|en|ang|crēopere}}, equivalent to {{af|en|creep|-er|id2=agent noun}}. Slang usage derived from phrase {{m|en|give the creeps}} or {{m|en|creep out}} (distinct from merely one who creeps).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɹipɚ/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-creeper.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːpə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person or a thing that [[crawl]]s or creeps.
#: {{syn|en|crawler}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1638|author=Robert Burton|title=w:The Anatomy of Melancholy|page=71|text=Standing Waters{{...}} are most unwholesome, putrified, and full of mites, '''creepers''', slimy, muddy, uncleane, corrupt, impure, by reason of the Suns heat, and still standing;|origyear=1621|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=hHNVAAAAcAAJ&pg=RA1-PA71}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2020-5-7|author=Katie Rife|title=If you’re looking to jump in your seat, make a playdate with Z|site=The Onion AV Club|url=https://film.avclub.com/if-you-re-looking-to-jump-in-your-seat-make-a-playdate-1843321861|passage=With his presence marked by shots of children’s toys overlaid with ominous music, Z is more of a '''creeper''' than a reaper—until a shocking, sudden moment midway through the film.}}
# {{lb|en|often|in the plural}} A one-piece [[garment]] for infants designed to facilitate access to the wearer's diaper.
#: {{syn|en|babygro|creepers|diaper shirt|infant bodysuit|onesie|snapsuit}}
# A device which allows a small child to safely roam around a room from a seated or standing position.
# A metal plate with [[spike|spikes]], designed to be worn with shoes to prevent [[slip|slipping]].
# A [[spur]]-like device strapped to the [[boot]] to facilitate [[climb]]ing. <!--not same as anti-slip shoe plate above-->
# {{lb|en|chiefly|in the plural}} A small low [[iron]], or [[dog]], between the [[andiron]]s.
# An instrument with iron hooks or claws for [[dredge|dredging]] up items from a [[well]] or other water.
# Any device for causing material to move steadily from one part of a [[machine]] to another, such as an [[apron]] in a [[carding]] machine, or an inner spiral in a grain screen.
# {{senseid|en|plant}} Any [[plant]] (as [[ivy]] or [[periwinkle]]) that grows by [[creep]]ing, especially a climbing plant of the genus {{taxfmt|Parthenocissus|genus}}.
#: {{syn|en|climber}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1964|author=w:William Golding|title=w:Lord of the Flies
|passage=Then the piglet tore loose from the '''creepers''' and scurried into the undergrowth.}}
# A [[treecreeper]].
# {{taxlink|Strophitus undulatus|species}}, a freshwater [[mussel]] of the eastern United States.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} A small four-hooked [[grapnel]] used to recover objects dropped onto the sea bed.
# The lowest gear of a tractor or truck.
#: {{synonyms|en|creeper gear|creeper shift}}
# {{senseid|en|low-profile wheeled platform for mechanic}} A low-profile wheeled [[platform]] whereupon an [[auto mechanic]] may lie on their back and gain better access to the underbody of a vehicle; a low stool similarly wheeled.
#: {{syn|en|q1=lie-down type|cradle}}
# {{senseid|en|person who creeps people out}} {{lb|en|pejorative|slang}} A person who [[creep someone out|creeps people out]]; a [[creepy]] person.
#: {{syn|en|creep#Noun|creepazoid#Noun|creepoid#Noun}}
#: ''Don't go to a nightclub to find a boyfriend. They're all '''creepers''' there.''
# A kind of [[shoe]], usually with a [[suede]] [[upper]] and a thick [[crepe]] [[sole]], associated with various 20th-century subcultures.
# {{lb|en|cricket}} A ball that travels low, near ground level.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author=Steven Lynch|title=Wisden on the Ashes|page=292
|passage=May joined Hutton and proceeded to play masterly cricket in which the straight-drive predominated. There was always the possibility that he might be trapped by a '''creeper''', but May watched the ball intently.}}

